codex
The lexical count is 12, but one call sits in an unreachable `else` after `len == 4` / `len != 4`. I also found a counterexample to the “common tail” claim: `memory_rw.c` zeroes the read buffer before calling the device, so `v0 == 0` cannot by itself prove the device wrote it at the tail.
