tools/pipeline/ledger.json:24842:     "outcome_note": "AND THE SIBLING SYMMETRY WARRANT IS WEAKER THAN MY BRIEF FRAMED IT.  I asked only whether anything reads re_tex.  The companion fact I omitted: **the three sibling TLB arrays ARE read** -- `tileptr = d->re_tlb_a[tile_nr] << 16' at dev_sgi_re.c:202, verified here, with a consumer-side bound above it.  So the siblings' `>>1' is LOAD-BEARING while TEX's scale governs write-only state.  'Make TEX match its siblings' is therefore consistency among stores only one of which anyone consults.",
tools/pipeline/ledger.json:24843:     "note": "AND THE SIBLING SYMMETRY WARRANT IS WEAKER THAN MY BRIEF FRAMED IT.  I asked only whether anything reads re_tex.  The companion fact I omitted: **the three sibling TLB arrays ARE read** -- `tileptr = d->re_tlb_a[tile_nr] << 16' at dev_sgi_re.c:202, verified here, with a consumer-side bound above it.  So the siblings' `>>1' is LOAD-BEARING while TEX's scale governs write-only state.  'Make TEX match its siblings' is therefore consistency among stores only one of which anyone consults."
